---
/**
 * Colophon — the quiet page behind the footer's "handcrafted" link.
 *
 * Static route rather than a pages-collection entry, deliberately: the pages
 * template ends in the Selected-work grid, which a colophon should not carry,
 * and adding an opt-out flag would mean a schema change mirrored into the
 * Tina config and lock. This reuses the overview template's classes only —
 * no fourth template, no new CSS.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Colophon — InfoDesignLab"
  description="What this site is made of, and how — typefaces, tools, and the care behind the graphs."
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="head">
      <div class="head__label">Colophon</div>
      <h1 class="head__title">Made the slow way</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="body">
      <aside class="rail">
        <strong><Icon name="corner-down-right" /> In short</strong>
        The small print — what this site is made of, and how.

        <br /><br />
        <strong><Icon name="corner-down-right" /> See also</strong>
        <a href="/co-design-process/">Co-design process</a>
        <br />
        <a href="mailto:post@infodesignlab.com">Contact</a>
        <br />
      </aside>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          Every visualisation on this site is real work, made for and with
          real people — scientists, policy-makers, editors, readers. Each one
          took hundreds of hours of dialogue before a single line settled.
          They are not always novel and not always surprising, but every one
          of them was designed with care, in collaborations that run from the
          scientific to the political.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is set in three typefaces and no more: a grotesque for
          headings and the homepage voice, Newsreader for the reading, and a
          monospace for the small print — including this rail. The canvas is
          a quiet grey; the menu blushes pink. If you select a sentence
          anywhere on the site, you will see the same pink.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is hand-coded — no theme, no template, every rule written for
          this site — built with Astro, edited through TinaCMS, and served by
          Netlify. Every change is a commit with an author and a diff, which
          feels right for a studio that believes understanding precedes
          action.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some of the details here are not meant to be noticed. But they are
          all meant to be felt. If you found this page, you look closely —{" "}
          <a href="mailto:post@infodesignlab.com">we should talk</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
